{"type":"text","text":"Done — mapped, proven, and promoted (3 new address entries; no ROM edits, so the ledger is still empty).\n\n## Results — Super Mario Bros. (World), World 1-1\n\n| Purpose | Address | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mario's horizontal speed | **`$0057`** | signed byte, **1/16 px per frame**; positive = right, negative = left (0x18 = 24 = 1.5 px/frame) |\n| Mario's vertical speed | **`$009F`** | signed byte, **px per frame**; negative = rising, positive = falling, 0 on the ground |\n| Direction he faces | **`$0033`** | **1 = right, 2 = left** |\n\n### Evidence\n**`$0057` — horizontal speed (watch).** The physics routine rewrites it every frame, so I proved it with a per-frame `play_input` watch. Held Right: `1,2,3,…,17`; switched to Left: `254,253,252,…,235` — it goes **negative** when Mario walks left. A 70-frame Right hold plateaued at exactly `24` (`$18`) while the X position `$0086` climbed 32→106 (~1.5 px/frame). No reference used.\n\n**`$009F` — vertical speed (watch).** Found by diffing a Start-pause-frozen grounded frame against a frozen mid-jump frame (`0 → 0xFD`). Through a full jump (A held 12 frames) it read `252,252,252(-4), 253,253,253(-3), 254(-2), 255(-1), 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4`, then `0` on landing — exactly tracking Y `$00CE` = 168 → 127 (apex) → 176.\n\n**`$0033` — facing (watch + write).** Two frozen standing states with opposite facing differed here (2 vs 1). A **one-frame** Right tap flipped it `2 → 1` on exactly the tap frame, the same frame Mario's OAM tile changed from the left pose (55/51) to the right pose (58/50). Write proof: while he stood facing right, `write_memory $0033 = 2` + 15 no-input frames kept it at 2 and flipped his OAM to the left pose (`list_sprites` returned `flip_h: true` for every Mario sprite, tiles 55/58/79).\n\n### Companions found along the way (noted, not promoted as separate entries)\n- **`$0700`** holds the *magnitude* of the horizontal speed (abs of `$0057`); `$0057` is the signed velocity Mario moves by.\n- **`$0045`** is the matching \"moving direction\" byte and is recomputed from the controller each frame (writing it was overwritten within one frame), unlike the persistent `$0033`.\n\nAll three are recorded with `record_mapping` (type address, confidence 1, source \"differential search\") and `promote_mappings` saved them to the ROM's mapping file."}
